    stress_p: 'With the rebuilt TQQQ (expense 0.84%, financing at T-bills + 0.51%) and liquidations on the close only, 1999-03 to 2010-02 (QQQ −1.3% a year, worst fall −83%): the base one-third hedge at 5x returned 4.9% a year at 5.0% volatility, worst fall −6.4%, +1.9 vs mix, 5.4 liquidations a year, liquidation-rule cost 2.1 points; 3x 6.2%, 1.7 a year, +3.2; hedge 0.2 at 5x 3.5% with a −41.6% worst fall; at zero funding 1.9% (−1.1). Episodes: the 1999 rally (QQQ +129.5%) base +9.8%, 3x +11.6%, hedge 0.2 +45.8%; the dot-com crash (−83%) +10.0% / +17.9% / −41.6%; the 2002–2007 recovery (+179%) +26.6% / +30.4% / +71.9%; 2008 (−53%) +7.3% / +8.8% / −19.7%; the 2009 rebound (+68%) +2.4% / +3.1% / +23.3%. The README’s “the 1999 rally liquidated it five times a year” was the 11-year average; the rally itself (1999-03-11 to 2000-03-27) liquidated the 5x position 13 times, about 12 a year (by calendar year: 1999 10, 2000 9, 2001 11, 2002 8, 2003 6, 2008 1, 2009 7).',

